.TH SEVERANCE 1 "2026-08" "severance" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
severance \- kernel-enforced work/personal boundary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B severance
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.br
.B work
.RI [ profile ]
.RI [ command ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B severance
provisions and audits a kernel-enforced boundary between confidential
(zero-data-retention) work and everything else on a single machine. Each
confidential context is a
.I profile
(an enclave): a Unix group, a sealed work tree owned
.BR root:<group> " mode " 2770
with a default ACL, and a matching account. A personal process, lacking the
group, is denied entry by the filesystem, not by convention.
.PP
.B work
enters an enclave: it acquires the group for the session via a human
.BR sudo (8)
prompt and runs a shell (or one command) with the enclave's account and
environment. Nothing persists.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install \fR/\fB uninstall
Standalone only: symlink the package into
.I ~/.local
and wire the git includeIf and the valet-key context shim (or remove them). A
guarded no-op under a host that already manages those.
.TP
.B list
List provisioned profiles;
.B *
marks the resolved default.
.TP
.BI show " [profile]"
Print the resolved settings for a profile (or the default).
.TP
.BI use " profile" "\fR|\fB --clear"
Set (or clear) the default-profile marker.
.TP
.BI init " name " [key=val ...]
Scaffold a new profile record under
.IR ~/.config/severance/profiles/ .
.TP
.BI seal " [profile...]"
Provision the boundary (group, sealed tree + ACLs, git identity). Privileged.
.TP
.BI runner " [profile...]"
Provision the per-enclave rootless-docker runner. Privileged.
.TP
.BI forget " profile " \fR[ \fB\-\-purge \fR]
Decommission a profile: tear down its runner (reversible). With
.B \-\-purge
also remove the record and regenerate the git fragment; the work tree is left
sealed. Privileged.
.TP
.BR check " [" \-\-seal | \-\-runner ]
Audit the live boundary; non-zero on drift. Bare checks both and validates the
records.
.TP
.BI validate " [profile]"
Lint profile records (parse, valid group, work_dir a subdir) before they
provision.
.TP
.B doctor
Whole-boundary health in one report: installation, records, integrations
(git includeIf, valet-key shim), and the live wall + runner.
.TP
.BR context " " resolve | guard
The valet-key discovery seam (resolve the active account; refuse a personal
account inside the work tree).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/severance/profiles/<name>
Profile records (key=value).
.TP
.I ~/.config/severance/default
The active-profile marker (written by
.BR "severance use" ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/git/work-context.gen
The generated git identity fragment.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WORK_PROFILE
Select a profile (overridden by an explicit argument).
.TP
.B SEVERANCE_PROFILES_DIR
Override the profiles directory (a host points this at its records).
.SH NOTES
The wall is the kernel. Permission lists and git config are not the boundary and
must not be relied on for it. The enclave group is transient: the login user is
never a permanent member. Entering the enclave is always a human sudo prompt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sudo (8),
.BR setfacl (1),
.BR git-config (1)
